Using the bundled `threejs-lighting` guide, replace it with this key-and-fill setup. Assumes the subject is centered at the origin, with Y up and viewed from +Z.

```js
export function illuminate(THREE, scene) {
  const key = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 1);
  key.position.set(5, 6, 5);
  key.target.position.set(0, 0, 0);

  const fill = new THREE.DirectionalLight(0xffffff, 0.35);
  fill.position.set(-5, 2, 4);
  fill.target.position.set(0, 0, 0);

  scene.add(key, key.target, fill, fill.target);
}
```

The elevated key defines form; the weaker opposite fill lifts dark-facing surfaces while preserving contrast. Call once during scene setup, replacing the existing ambient-light call. Shadows remain disabled, so this requires no renderer or mesh changes.

